Hi All,

Thanks for the quick answer (as usual :). I am sorry to confuse some, I
don't mean it's a snapshot from the advfs (or snapshot from storagework
term.) But I got the right answer. The best one is, from: Davis, Alan


Use something like :

find / -type d -ls

or 

find / -type d -exec /usr/bin/getacl -D {} \;

There are also scripts available on the 'net that will display a
directory as a tree structure. You could modify one of them to show the
permissions or ACLs.

Alan Davis

