Re. generating coredump:
Thanks to:
Dave Simmonds: - kill -3 pid
Joe Fletcher : - run Netscape ;-)
Michael Maxie : - 
name the program core.c
--------------8<-----------------------------
#include <assert.h>

int main(int argc,
        char **argv)
{

        assert(1);
        exit(0);

}




--------------8<-----------------------------

$ cc core.c
$ ./a.out


Thanks to Robert Mulley.

Solution:

sysconfig -q proc (shows current attribute values)

sysconfig -r proc enhanced-core-name=1 (to change it from 0 to 1)
enhanced-core-name: reconfigured

sysconfig -q proc (shows current attribute values again to confirm)

I haven't tested this yet (does anyone know of an easy way to generate a
core dump?).

Rgds,

Tony.


Original posting:
Hi,

I recall that there is a way to give unique names to core dumps (kernel
attribute?) , but don't remember how.
TU4.0Dpk3.

TIF,

Tony.


 
 
 
 
