From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Jun 22 14:18:14 2001
From: bryan.mills () lynx ! co ! uk
Date: Fri, 22 Jun 2001 14:18:14 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: ADVFS Performance
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653649622022

My original post was as follows,

 --------------------------------------------------------------------------=20=
 --
" I am setting up a  DS20 server (TRU64 4=2E0F) with a RAID Array 8000
attached using a HSZ80 SCSI controller=2E  I have created a file domain
with a series of filesets mounted up using ADVFS to store large numbers
of small files=2E  There will be a fileset for each month, and then a
directory beneath that for each day=2E  Typically each daily directory will=20=


store 90,000 to 100,000 small files in it
When copying large volumes of data to these filesets I am seeing a very
noticable degredation in performance as the copy progresses=2E"


Several people noted that ADVFS is not very good at handling a large=20=
number files in this manner, it was suggested that this has been improved=20=
in V5=2E1=2E  This upgrade is possible at the present time=2E  Respondants also=20=
suggested converting to using UFS, and to pay particular attention to=20=
inode configuration=2E

The compaq guide for ADVFS notes some changes which can be made to the=20=
'makefdmn' syntax to try and eliminate the problem=2E

The location for this document is as follows,

http://www=2Etru64unix=2Ecompaq=2Ecom/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/H=20=
TML/ADVFS_html/figures/admin-chap2=2Ehtml#TofC51

Brenden Phillips suggested creating a deeper directory structure and=20=
storing files by the hour, rather than by the day=2E  This led us to some=20=
testing where each file was stored in a sub-directory corresponding to=20=
the last two digits of the file name, so file 1223443201 goes to=20=
/2001/06/20/01, 1223443202 goes to /2001/06/20/02, and so forth=2E  As the=20=
files are created with sequential numbers, this gives us a good even=20=
spread of files across 100 sub-directories=2E  It was however noted that=20=
having the directory structure too deep could negate this improvement=2E

The performance benefits from this change have been quite staggering=2E=20=
  An overnight job which copies the files onto the server was running=20=
until 8am each morning=2E  It is now finishing before midnight the previous=20=
evening=2E

Thanks to all who responded=2E  Looks like we have a good result on this=20=
one, with further avenues to explore if required=2E

Regards,

Bryan Mills=2E=20=


