> 
> If you do this, what then is the procedure if you forget the 
> root password? Is there some other way to recover use of the 
> root account?

Most of the responses called for booting from CD and modifying the passwd
file to remove the root password.

Probably the cleanest suggestion was to boot from CD and edit /etc/rc.config
to modify SECURE_CONSOLE, since that would work regardless of what type of
security is in place.

Thanks to all who responded. My curiosity is now satisfied (at least about
this issue).
