I would like to configure separate oracle homes so that Oracle installer
doesn't corrupt the installation 
(when you specify the other cluster node during the install). Oracle
documentation and Metalink don't adequately address this issue and I didn't
find anything in the archives. 

Has anyone used cdsl's or ??? so that the Oracle installer successfully
installs in two separate homes? Metalink had a work around by doing two
separate installs. Seems that Oracle needs to provide better support for
tru64 ops installs.

We have been using a common cluster disk for the installs and decided that
separate homes will enable us to do patches on one home while keeping the
other instance available for users.


Thanks, 

Bob Safran
