To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Custom printer scripts
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653649621918
MIME-Version: 1
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="--1036700-20760-992935712=:295"

--1036700-20760-992935712=:295
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; CHARSET=US-ASCII
Content-Language: en-USA

Thank you to all that responded to my request for help.

As Kevin Flemming pointed out to me, the problem was with PK3 on version 5.1 of
Tru64.  Once I removed "Patch 0030.00 Introduces the JJ printcap parameter"
from my system, my custom printer scripts worked perfectly.

Most of the responses I received also recommended that the "if" printcap
parameter be used to call scripts as this usually works well.

Kind Regards 

Rahveen Ramnath
Unilever South Africa, Durban
