Subject: SUMMARY: Error: swat/tcp: bind: Address already in use
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653649621835

Tru64 Managers:

Thanks for the assistance provided.

Suggestions:
1. Use /usr/local/bin/lsof -i to find a list of all ports that are in use.

2. Use a different port for swat (change in /etc/services )
(This might help "hide" swat from the "bad guys".)

3. Run Samba GUI (swat) on a non-privileged port number [but there's a
warning about a possible security risk]



Rob Aldridge
AT&T Solutions
Alliance, Ohio

-----Original Message-----
Tru64 Managers:

I'm experiencing the following error message repeatedly on a Tru64 5.1
system:
	inetd[1049417]: swat/tcp: bind: Address already in use

A similar posting was made to this Tru64 mailing list last year, but there
is no summary of the resolution.

'swat' is the SAMBA graphical user interface that lives at port 901.   I
understand that this may also be the port that mountd also uses.

My question is, how to avoid this error?   Can I simply pick a new port
number for the 'swat' interface?
Or can I tell mountd not to use 901 ?



Thank you,

Rob Aldridge
AT&T Solutions
Alliance, Ohio

