Hi all,

Thanks *very* much for the quick and numerous replies.
For everbody else's benefit, here's a summary of what
I've learnt from the replies:

Any ECC Unbuffered SDRAM 168pin, installed in pairs
upto 256 MB/module, 3 pairs max will work. Speed
100MHz atleast, or more. 66 MHz might be slow.

Suggested vendors are "Crucial.com", configsys.com
Computer Clearinghouse in NY, Compugen Systems ON,
CPU Options <cpuoptions.com> etc.

Prices seem to be around $325+ for a 512 MB Kit
(2x256)
and and $160 for a 256MB Kit (2x128).

Thanks very much everybody, for the very qiuck reply.
I'll contact one of these vendors and get the RAM.

