From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Jun 12 17:05:08 2001
From: "Karen R. McArthur" <kmcarthu () bates ! edu>
Date: Tue, 12 Jun 2001 17:05:08 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Insight Manager on Tru64 4.0g
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653649621793

This list is GREAT!  Thanks for all the quick responses.

I found this software after installing 4.0g, but others have found it in
4.0f (we skipped over that version).  General consensus is to disable
Insight Manager due to bugs (see www.securityfocus.com -> search BUGTRAQ
for -> insight manager).

There are a few ways to disable this:
1.) if you have applied patch of at least CPQIM211, you can disable it in
/etc/rc.config with INSIGHTD_CONF="no"
2.) move the insightd script out of /sbin/init.d
3.) close port 2301
4.) rename /sbin/rc3.d/S..insight... to something "non-startable"

In all of these scenarios, you will probably need to shut down the currently
running insightd (/sbin/init.d/insightd stop).

Many thanks to J. Bacher, sysadmin@astro.su.se, Nikola Milutinovic and
Edward J. Branley.
--
