Subject: Tru64 on Alpha PC164
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653649621744

Thanks to all those who replied so quickly! Kurt Ludwig sent me the following
solution that did the trick:

------

this Motherboard *WILL* run Tru64 once you get srm on it.

the PC164 series motherboards are 1/2 flash boards. This means you can have
either SRM OR AlphaBIOS/ARC in the firmware prom, but not both at the same
time.

you can update the machine to SRM as such:

get the PC164 firmware image at:
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/alphapc164.html

rename the file to pc164nt.rom (instead of pc164srm.rom). This way AlphaBIOS
will think it's an AlphaBIOS image and update to it.

[ JG: The floppy should have pc164nt.rom and fwupdate.exe in the ]
[ top level directory. ]

