Hi all,

I only received one reply on my question (See below) and it was another
question. Our own investigation so far suggests, nothing. No idea. Nadda! 

Our call to Compaq came back with "next time take a crash dump" and they
closed the call. 

For those who don't know. If the machine hangs. Halt it with the reset
switch. at the "P0>>>" prompt type in "crash" then reboot normally. This
will create a crash dump file which can then be forwarded to Compaq for
analysis. As it was the other log files (/var/adm/messages,
/var/adm/binary.log and /var/adm/syslog.dated...) gave no indication as the
reason for the hang. The only advise from Compaq? Next time get a crash
dump.

So now we sit and wait. The only other thing to add is that since this seems
to happen on a reasonably regular basis, 3 times in the last 6 months, I
think we may just be able to get that crash dump for Compaq to analyse.

