happened on Sunday morning, with a second panic 10 minutes after the first 
reboot.  It happened again on Monday evening, when it rebooted multiple 
times over the course of approximately 50 minutes, not staying up for more 
than 10 minutes between reboots.  It finally stayed running, and ran 
throughout the night and all day, without fail, with the normal user load 
consisting of some 300 - 500 concurrent users.  Review of the DECEvent logs 
show the same/similar errors trapped each time.  Relevant entries are in the 
attached text file.

The configuration is as follows:
Tru64 Unix version 4.0E
3 GB Memory
4- 5/600 8MB CPU
1- BA356 shelf containing (2) swap disks and (2)OS disks (LSM Mirror)
1- RaidArray 7000, fully populated with 9 & 18 GB, 7200 & 10K RPM drives

RA contains multiple filesystems for HOME directories, application 
executables, and databases.
All filesystems are ADVFS.

The panic is occuring on either CPU 3 or CPU 0 and indicates a System 
Uncorrectable Machine Check
Machine Check Reason          x0202  IOD-Detected Hard Error -OR-
