------=_NextPart_000_0042_01C0ED4B.CC4814E0
Content-Type: text/plain;
	charset="iso-8859-1"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

A big thanks to Thomas Leitner, Thomas Blinn and Graham Allan.
---Orginal message---

Hi managers.
=20
I have a question about the new 3Dlabs Oxygen VX1 PCI adapter.
=20
Does Tru64 have OpenGL (hardware acceleration) for this graphic card?=20
=20
And how about the 2D preformance?=20
If anyone have a Oxygen adapter, can you run x11perf -circle100 and give =
me the results?=20
I have a PS300 in my PWS and its realy poor 2D graphics.
=20
--End of Orginal message--


2D preformance:
=20
Graham Allan says:

The VX1 is much, much better for 2D than the previous entry-level ELSA
GLoria Synergy.

Here's the result from x11perf on a XP900 (466MHz) workstation, running
Tru64 5.1 patchkit 3, running X at 1600x1200 in 24-bits:

40000 reps @   0.1934 msec (  5170.0/sec): 100-pixel circle

And Thomas Blinn:
=20
2D performance is slightly better than the ELSA GLoria Synergy/Comet
card that the VX1 replaces.  For 1024x768 8-bit color, it gets about
23 Xmarks.  16-bit performance seems optimal for this card; it gets
24 Xmarks (at 1024x768) in 16-bit truecolor mode.  24-bit truecolor
mode drops the performance to about 14 Xmarks at 1024x768.

I run my own VX1 card at 1280x1024 16-color mode.  For the -circle100
test, I get 5260/second over a total of 200000 reps.
=20
3D hardware support.
=20
Thomas Blinn:

No, we will not be supporting OpenGL on the VX1, either with or without
hardware acceleration.

=20
Last comment:
=20
Seems to this is the fastest 2D Compaq/Tru64 graphic card right now.
It had be realy nice if Compaq could make a fast 2D graphics card with =
3D (OpenGL) hardware support under Tru64/OVMS and Linux.=20

/regards=20
Olle Hansson
=20

